// "Fight" ([CR#701.14a]): two creatures each deal damage equal to their power
// to the other, simultaneously. NOT a primitive verb — a macro over `DealDamage`.
//
// - [CR#701.14b] both-or-neither: the `If` guard fires the batch only when BOTH
//   fighters are still creatures on the battlefield (`Creature` = a creature
//   permanent). If either isn't, `then` never runs — neither deals damage, and
//   `Composite`'s `KeywordActionPerformed{Fight}` is suppressed (no fight, no
//   "fights" trigger).
// - simultaneity: the `Simultaneously` batch — both halves read the pre-damage
//   powers and land together, SBAs after the whole batch.
// - [CR#701.14c] self-fight: same object both sides → two `X -> X` packets, which
//   the engine coalesces (same source+target in one batch) into ONE 2x instance.
// - [CR#701.14d] fight damage is never combat damage (`DealDamage`'s default).
//
// Each half spells its source explicitly (`DealDamage(source, amount, target)`),
// so the dealer is that same creature (deathtouch/lifelink attribution, Pounce
// redirect). `Creature` inlined as `And([Permanent, Type("Creature")])` to avoid
// a nested macro in a macro body.
//
// Usage: Fight(a, b) — e.g. Fight(Target(0), Target(1)).
(
    name: "Fight",
    template: "${0} fights ${1}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Reference, Reference],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Fight",
        body: If(
            condition: And([
                Matches(Param(0), And([Permanent, Type("Creature")])),
                Matches(Param(1), And([Permanent, Type("Creature")])),
            ]),
            then: Simultaneously([
                DealDamage(Param(0), StatOf(Param(0), Power), Param(1)),
                DealDamage(Param(1), StatOf(Param(1), Power), Param(0)),
            ]),
        ),
    ),
)
